  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "It targets .NET Standard 2.0 and higher version. Supports double, float, Half and complex numbers. On .NET 11 and higher, also supports generic Complex<T> (Decimal32, Decimal64, Decimal128, float, Half, BFloat16, double). Breaking change: complex functions now return principal values with IEEE 754 / C99 branch-cut conventions, identical on all .NET versions; improved accuracy for extreme arguments.",
